 didn't take one in the quarterback draft  in the previous year  you've got a great running back and say  Quan Barkley but now you're stuck with  Eli and is last year and really no plan  moving forward  yeah it's an interesting dynamic because  I don't think Eli's ever gone into the  final year of a deal you know it's not  like the Giants to have their  quarterback kind of going into that mode  but I look at it like what we heard  gentlemen say and what we heard  schirmer's say you know at the combine  look we're counting on Eli this year and  I think the hope is that this team is  better that they win games make it to  the postseason and I think the hope is  that UI has a good year and they make  and it makes them have a tough decision  going forward I think that would be a  great problem to have if you're Dave  gentlemen but I also think they look at  well if you didn't fall in love with one  of the quarterbacks from last year I  don't know that I see it happening this  year unless you've got the number one  pick and I think they look at that and  say look maybe we take a quarterback  later on the giraffe but there isn't  somebody that they're ready to go all-in  on and when you look at the Giants and  when the season ended the first thing  that come out of the gentleman's mouth  was we've got to fix our defense we've  got to find a way to stop people get  after the quarterback this draft is  loaded with guys that can do just that  and now the fact that they were able to  pick up an extra first-round pick and  that's a third round pick I could see  them making a complete overhaul that  defense yeah I'm just not sure what  they're doing with gold and Tate you  know he's a nice second or third  receiver there and you're paying him  some pretty good money there I I don't  know I think you're either all-in on  let's rebuild get maybe the top draft  pick next year you know I don't want to  use the word tanking we don't use that  me NFL but that would be what I would be  doing I would just say all right we're  gonna pave the way and to a tongue of  Eylau is gonna be our quarterback next  year and let's just then then we start  our rebuild because I thought with Odell  and say Kwan I'd go all in on Kyler  murmuring I would make that offense  something we had never seen I'd make you  have to prepare for us and I would turn  the NFL on its ear that would have been  my approach if I was the Giants and I  was keeping everybody the defense under  they underperformed and but I would have  a dynamic offense is that asking too  much is that too far-fetched for the  Giants organization to think that way  well I think it sounds good on paper you  know and I mean that's certainly the  Cleveland model I mean that's what  they're going for they've got Baker  they've got obj they got Jarvis you know  they've gotten Joko you know I think  when I look at the Giants offense you  know I look at him innit  they had to have said all right you know  I personally don't think they were  shopping Odell but I think they got an  offer from the Browns who you know John  Dorsey took a shot and he said look what  happens and they said man we you know we  can't turn this down we've got it we've  got to make moves because the reality is  we didn't win a lot of games with Odell  went to the playoffs one time you know  you look at you know I mean who are the  top five receiver in the NFL right now  you know did any of them make the  playoffs that were any of them in the  Super Bowl you know yeah I think you  look at it like if the fact that the  Giants have sake won Berkeley that's  what enabled them to make this trade and  to make this move this offense is going  to be centered around him Golden State's  gonna be a piece of that sterling  Shepherds gonna be a part of that  everything was going to be a part of  that but you know there are people in  that building that actually felt like  wow this offense was actually pretty  good  without Odell at the end of the season  you know he didn't play the last I think  four games of the season and you know  look I think they got a little glimpse  of that you know the year before I was  hurt and I was at the bar code but this  offense you know I think as many points  is you want to score it doesn't do any  good if you're not you can't get off the  field on defense and if you can't find a  way to stop people Sean good to visit  with you as always we appreciate your  time  thanks Dan appreciate it man have a good  weekend and Shawn O'Hara NFL Network  analyst former Super Bowl champ with a  change for more Dan Patrick show to the  audience Channel 239 on DirecTV or  download the Dan Patrick show app  [Music]

